// cppcheck suppressions: one per intentional violation.
// Format: <id>:<file>:<line>  followed by `// audit:<ID> <rationale>`.
// File-wide form `<id>:<file>` and project-wide `<id>:*` also accepted.
//
// Every entry names a file that $(SRC) actually compiles.  The core
// re-foundation deleted nine blocks here whose files went with the old
// runtime -- the computed-goto dispatch table, the object-model lookup
// stamps, the unwinder's pattern stub, the watcher eval-pass counter, the
// loader strand.  A suppression for a file cppcheck cannot see is not
// harmless: it reads as a known exception when it is a fossil.
//
// Common categories to expect:
//   missingIncludeSystem  — system includes intentionally not parsed
//   unusedFunction        — public C API consumed by tests/ + external embedders
//                           (cppcheck scans src/ only — every public-API entry
//                           point looks unused from its perspective)
//   constParameterCallback— argv const-cast would cascade into every callback
//                           function-pointer site; cppcheck flags this itself

// =============================================================================
// Project-wide: unusedFunction (Phase 19)
// =============================================================================
// audit:CPPCHK-009 (Phase 19) — cppcheck scans src/ only; the public C API
// surface (urbi_*, helper definitions used by tests/, native callbacks invoked
// via function-pointer tables) is structurally unreachable from cppcheck's
// call-graph view.  Suppressing the whole category project-wide is correct
// here: removing or marking-static any public-API symbol would break
// test/ binaries or external embedders.  Re-evaluate if cppcheck gains
// cross-TU resolution for header-declared exports.
unusedFunction

// =============================================================================
// Per-site suppressions
// =============================================================================

// audit:CPPCHK-011 (Phase 19) — pattern_matches() is an M3 catch-everything
// stub that always returns 1 (src/runtime/uunwind.c:65 docstring); cppcheck
// correctly flags the call-site as `always true`.  M5 refines pattern dispatch
// to actual exception-class matching (see comment block at uunwind.c:55-62);
// suppressing keeps the gate green until that lands.
//
// CPPCHK-001 (defer:M6) is the same finding under a different ID — filed
// before CPPCHK-011 from a different cppcheck pass and resolved transitively
// when Phase 19 closed CPPCHK-011.  Both close at v0.6.1-stdlib (Phase 12).
// Line-pinned entry knownConditionTrueFalse:src/runtime/uunwind.c:313 removed
// (v0.13.6 comment-sweep shifted pattern_matches call-site; file-wide entry at
// knownConditionTrueFalse:src/runtime/uunwind.c below covers it).

// audit:CPPCHK-012 (Phase 19, closed Phase 9) — constParameterCallback
// previously fired on event_sync_emit_method in uevent_native.c when
// the callback function-pointer type was registered via event_native_register.
// Subsequent refactoring moved the callback to direct-call registration;
// cppcheck no longer detects the pattern.  Suppression retired.

// audit:CPPCHK-013 (Phase 19, updated Phase 6, retired v0.8.0) — parse_err_line /
// parse_err_col suppressions retired: v0.8.0 Task 8 refactored urbi_run_chunk to
// use persistent loader strands, moving the parse-error path.  Under current
// cppcheck version, the pattern (write in freestanding, read in __STDC_HOSTED__)
// no longer triggers unreadVariable warnings; modern cppcheck tracks
// configuration-conditional paths more precisely.  Suppressions removed.

// audit:CPPCHK-Phase5 — src/stdlib/atoms.c's DEF_INT_BINOP macro
// expands to native-method callbacks whose signature is pinned by the
// urbi_native_method_fn typedef (UVM *vm, UValue self, UValue *args,
// uint8_t nargs, UValue *out).  cppcheck flags `args` as constable
// because the macro body only reads args[0]; const-casting would
// cascade through every native-method registration site.  Mirrors the
// rationale at CPPCHK-012 above.
constParameterPointer:src/stdlib/atoms.c

// audit:CPPCHK-Phase6 (retired at the containers re-foundation) — the
// constParameterPointer / constVariablePointer entries covered locals
// that list_storage / dict_storage / dict_lookup handed back out of the
// `_storage` slot.  Those helpers and that slot are gone: a receiver is
// a UList / UDict cell reached straight off the value, and every
// read-only local is already const.  What is left is the callback
// signature itself, covered by the audit:refound-task9 block below.

// audit:CPPCHK-Phase7 — src/stdlib/runtime_types.c native-method callbacks
// expose UValue *args as part of the urbi_native_method_fn typedef; the
// Exception primitive's exc_new only reads args[0] so cppcheck flags it,
// but the function-pointer signature is pinned and cannot be const-qualified
// without breaking every callback registration site.
// (retired at the re-foundation: cppcheck now reports these sites with the
// Callback spelling, covered by the refound-task9 block at the end.)

// audit:CPPCHK-Phase9 — src/stdlib/primitives.c native-method callbacks
// (Mutex / Date / Duration .new / .fromSeconds / .fromMicroseconds / .plus)
// expose UValue *args via the urbi_native_method_fn typedef; same rationale
// as Phase 7 — the function-pointer signature is pinned.
// (retired at the re-foundation: same Callback-spelling move as
// runtime_types.c above.)

// (src/stdlib/debug_namespace.c's entry retired at the re-foundation:
// the namespace is one method now and its unused args are cast away.)

// audit:v094-repl-portability — src/repl/urepl_queue.c uses UREPL_MUTEX_LOCK /
// UREPL_COND_WAIT / UREPL_COND_BROADCAST macros (from src/repl/urepl_threading.h)
// that expand to pthread_mutex_lock / pthread_cond_wait / pthread_cond_broadcast
// on POSIX builds.  Cppcheck doesn't model the macro-hidden pthread semantics:
//   - constParameterPointer: cppcheck thinks `q` / `rb` could be const because
//     the macro takes &q->mutex (a member-address) rather than mutating q
//     directly — but pthread_mutex_lock DOES mutate the mutex (and so q's
//     contents).  Const-qualifying would fail to compile (pthread takes non-
//     const).
//   - knownConditionTrueFalse: cppcheck doesn't model pthread_cond_wait's
//     "release mutex, wait, reacquire mutex" semantics, so the post-wait
//     check of q->inited (set false during shutdown by another thread) looks
//     dead.
// Surfaced by the v0.9.4 typedef-shim swap (commit a8f121c) which replaced
// direct pthread_* calls with UREPL_* macros; the new indirection broke
// cppcheck's flow analysis.
// (src/repl/urepl_queue.c is PARKED and not in $(SRC), so cppcheck never
// scans it; these two entries come back with the networked server.)
// constParameterPointer:src/repl/urepl_queue.c
// knownConditionTrueFalse:src/repl/urepl_queue.c

// (src/repl/urepl_dispatch.c's entry retired at the re-foundation: the
// handler it covered was dispatch_auth, which went with the networked
// server, and the live handlers already take a const request.)

// audit:v0.12.5-m10-prep — src/stdlib/regexp.c native-method callbacks
// (regexp_new / regexp_match / etc.) expose UValue *args via the
// urbi_native_method_fn typedef.  Same rationale as Phase 5/6/7/9 above —
// the function-pointer signature is pinned and cannot be const-qualified
// without breaking every native-method registration site.
constParameterPointer:src/stdlib/regexp.c

// audit:v0.12.0-ros (retired v0.13.6) — constParameterCallback:src/ros/uros.c
// was added at v0.12.0 under the assumption cppcheck would flag the
// native-method callbacks with the constParameterCallback check ID.  In
// practice cppcheck emits constParameterPointer for these sites (not
// constParameterCallback); the entry never matched and cppcheck reports it
// as unmatchedSuppression.  The constParameterPointer suppression below
// (audit:v0.12.0-ros-R1 / // (PARKED with the rest of src/ros/; not in $(SRC).)
// constParameterPointer:src/ros/uros.c) already covers
// all live findings; this entry is deleted rather than corrected to avoid a
// duplicate.

// audit:v0.12.0-ros-R1 — src/ros/uros.c urbi_ros_shutdown(vm) uses `vm` only
// for the owner-equality check (b->owner != vm); cppcheck suggests
// `const struct UVM *`.  The public C API surface in include/urbi/ros.h pins
// `struct UVM *vm` to match urbi_ros_pump / urbi_ros_register / urbi_ros_*
// uniformity (same rationale as the v0.10.9-W3 urbi_tag_block suppression for
// uunwind.c above).  Const-qualifying would break API uniformity and force
// callers through a const-cast.
// (PARKED with the rest of src/ros/; not in $(SRC).)
// constParameterPointer:src/ros/uros.c

// audit:v0.13.6-namespace-day — src/emit/uemit_internal.h patch_fwd_jmp_here(UEmitter *e, ...)
// urbi_emit_patch_instr() mutates the emitter's instruction buffer; cppcheck cannot see through
// the opaque UEmitter* and flags 'e' as constable.  Same rationale as atoms.c et al above.
constParameterPointer:src/emit/uemit_internal.h:184

// audit:v0.13.6-namespace-day — src/parse/uparse_stmt.c urbi_parse_function uses block-scoped
// `UAstNode *err = NULL` inside `{ }` expect() one-liners; the outer `err` (reject_bare_function_forms
// result) is a completely different variable at function scope.  The pattern is used at every
// expect() call site in this file and cannot be removed without restructuring all callers.
shadowVariable:src/parse/uparse_stmt.c:771
shadowVariable:src/parse/uparse_stmt.c:788
shadowVariable:src/parse/uparse_stmt.c:812

// audit:refound-task9 — every src/stdlib file defines native
// methods whose signature is pinned by the boot table's UMethodDef:
//   int (*)(UVM *, UValue self, UValue *args, uint8_t nargs, UValue *out)
// A body that only READS args[0] draws constParameterCallback, but
// const-qualifying one body would need a cast at its table entry and
// would then diverge from every other row.  Same rationale as the
// per-file constParameterPointer entries above; cppcheck emits the
// Callback spelling for these because it can see the function-pointer
// table in the same translation unit or its header.
constParameterCallback:src/stdlib/lobby_native.c
constParameterCallback:src/stdlib/object_root.c
constParameterCallback:src/stdlib/atoms.c
constParameterCallback:src/stdlib/containers.c
constParameterCallback:src/stdlib/namespaces.c
constParameterCallback:src/stdlib/primitives.c
constParameterCallback:src/stdlib/regexp.c
constParameterCallback:src/stdlib/runtime_types.c
// Same signature, same reason: rt/usched_natives.c holds the Tag, Event
// and Job method tables and the scheduler globals.
constParameterCallback:src/rt/usched_natives.c

// audit:rt-threaded-dispatch — src/rt/uexec_ops.c builds its computed-goto
// label table by expanding src/chunk/uopcodes.def into `&&L_<op>,` rows.
// cppcheck cannot parse a list of label addresses and reports a syntaxError
// at the first row of the .def, which aborts only the __GNUC__ configuration
// of that file; the switch configuration of the same opcode bodies is still
// analysed in full.  The .def holds nothing but X-macro rows, so a real
// syntax error in it would stop the compiler long before this gate.
syntaxError:src/chunk/uopcodes.def
